      en: "Kuajok Stadium is a modern sports facility in Kuajok, Warrap State, South Sudan. Opened in 2010, it was built with FIFA funding and features an artificial turf pitch and a 400-meter running track. The stadium has a capacity of 4,000 spectators and is equipped with floodlights for night games. It is the home ground of Kuajok United FC, a club in the South Sudan Premier League. In 2012, the stadium hosted the Warrap State Football Championship final. The facility includes changing rooms, a gym, and a conference room. The artificial turf is made of recycled materials and requires minimal maintenance. Kuajok Stadium symbolizes the commitment to sports development in post-conflict South Sudan.",
